# ${project.name}

Maven Reporting Implementation provides
[`AbstractMavenReport`](./apidocs/org/apache/maven/reporting/AbstractMavenReport.html), the base class for report
plugins. A report that extends it runs in two ways:

1. as part of **site generation**, when the [Maven Site Plugin](/plugins/maven-site-plugin/) calls it through the
   [Maven Reporting API](../maven-reporting-api/)'s
   [`MavenReport`](../maven-reporting-api/apidocs/org/apache/maven/reporting/MavenReport.html) interface.
2. as a **standalone goal**, for example `mvn myreport:report`, through the Maven Plugin API's
   [`Mojo`](/ref/current/maven-plugin-api/apidocs/org/apache/maven/plugin/Mojo.html) interface. The report then
   renders its own HTML page with the site skin from the project's `src/site/site.xml`, or, with
   `-Doutput.format=<format>` such as `xdoc` or `apt`, writes the report in that Doxia format without a skin.

Either way, `AbstractMavenReport` calls your `executeReport(Locale)` method, which writes the report through
`getSink()`. Reports with several pages create a sink for each extra page with `getSinkFactory()`.

The [guide to developing a report plugin](/guides/plugin/guide-java-report-plugin-development.html) walks through a
complete example. The integration tests in this repository hold a working report plugin:
[`src/it/setup-reporting-plugin`](https://github.com/apache/maven-reporting-impl/tree/${project.scm.tag}/src/it/setup-reporting-plugin).

${esc.h}${esc.h} Which Doxia version runs

The Doxia version used at runtime differs between the two modes:

1. During **site generation**, the Maven Site Plugin provides Doxia and the Reporting API to the report, overriding
   the plugin's own dependencies; see
   [`DefaultMavenReportExecutor`](/shared/maven-reporting-exec/apidocs/org/apache/maven/reporting/exec/DefaultMavenReportExecutor.html)
   in [Maven Reporting Exec](/shared/maven-reporting-exec/).
2. As a **standalone goal**, the report uses the Doxia version it depends on, which comes in transitively through
   this library.

Code a report against the oldest Maven Site Plugin you support; the
[Reporting API compatibility notes](../maven-reporting-api/index.html${esc.hash}Compatibility_notes_for_report_authors)
list the current pitfalls.

${esc.h}${esc.h} Upgrading to 4.1.0

Version 4.1.0 builds on Reporting API 4.1.0, Doxia 2.2.0 and Doxia Sitetools 2.1.0. Recompile your report against
it; two changes can affect subclasses:

- The protected field `siteRenderer` and the method `getSiteRenderer()` now use the type `SiteRenderer` instead of the
  deprecated `Renderer`. An override that returns the field must declare `SiteRenderer` as its return type.
- A new parameter, `mavenSession`, holds the Maven session. The site descriptor of a standalone report is now
  interpolated with user and system properties too, as the Maven Site Plugin already does.

Multi-page reports keep working with Maven Site Plugin 3.22.0 and older: `AbstractMavenReport` still implements the
deprecated `MavenMultiPageReport` interface, which those versions require.

